From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>
Date: Thu, 6 May 2021 00:12:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Compile out NUMA code entirely when NUMA is
 disabled

Scheduler code is very hot and every little optimization counts. Instead
of constantly checking sched_numa_balancing from task_tick_fair() when NUMA
is disabled, compile it out.

Signed-off-by: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index d7ec236ec521c89b617ba1d0c36b2f08992078b9..675302d5e2711ef2c2eace60ec5638a11d8f4b93 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -4459,10 +4459,6 @@ static void update_scan_period(struct task_struct *p, int new_cpu)
 
 #else /* !CONFIG_NUMA_BALANCING: */
 
-static void task_tick_numa(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *curr)
-{
-}
-
 static inline void account_numa_enqueue(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *p)
 {
 }
@@ -14874,8 +14870,10 @@ static void task_tick_fair(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *curr, int queued)
 	if (queued)
 		return;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_NUMA_BALANCING
 	if (static_branch_unlikely(&sched_numa_balancing))
 		task_tick_numa(rq, curr);
+#endif /* CONFIG_NUMA_BALANCING */
 
 	task_tick_cache(rq, curr);
 
